    "alert_id": "EX2_002",
    "title": "TDF renal monitoring gap during acute illness",
    "message": "Guidelines require serum creatinine and eGFR monitoring every 12 months for patients on TDF. The last creatinine was 375 days ago. While today's creatinine is available, no eGFR has been calculated. During acute kidney injury, serial creatinine monitoring is essential to track recovery or deterioration after IV fluid resuscitation. The clinician's plan does not include repeat renal function testing.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Calculate eGFR now and repeat serum creatinine daily during admission to monitor AKI recovery and guide TDF re-initiation timing.",
    "citations": [
