    ]
  },
  {
    "alert_id": "EX2_003",
    "title": "Plan lacks ART continuity strategy",
    "message": "If TDF is held during acute kidney injury, the clinician's plan does not address maintaining viral suppression. DTG and 3TC are not contraindicated in AKI. Guidelines suggest substituting TDF with an alternative such as TAF or AZT if TDF is contraindicated. The plan should specify whether DTG and 3TC will be continued and what TDF replacement will be used if discontinuation is confirmed after recovery.",
    "issue_type": "plan_review",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Continue DTG and 3TC during AKI. If TDF is permanently stopped, substitute with TAF or AZT per guidelines once renal function stabilises.",
